$ diva run sum.ml
55
[exit 0]

$ diva check sum.ml
no runtime error is possible
[exit 0]

$ diva opt sum.ml
(let rec sum n = (if (n <= 0) then 0 else (n + (sum (n - 1)))) in (sum 10))
[exit 0]

$ diva hints sum.ml
n#1 : [0, 10]
$sum#0 : [0, +∞]
[exit 0]

$ diva cert --check sum.ml
[diva] running Lean on sum.lean
wrote sum.lean
certificate checked by Lean: the program never fails
[exit 0]

$ diva prove --check -o prove.lean sum.ml
[diva] running Lean on prove.lean
wrote prove.lean
checked by Lean: the functions meet their contracts, and the top-level expressions don't fail
[exit 0]

